course: dictionary
lesson: 3261
title: The equator
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The equator is an imaginary line drawn around the middle of the Earth, halfway between the North Pole and the South Pole. You cannot see it on the ground, but it is drawn on maps and globes.
explain: The equator divides the Earth into two halves, the Northern Hemisphere and the Southern Hemisphere. «Near the equator the Sun is always high, so it is warm all year and the seasons are weak.»
explain: Places on opposite sides of the equator have opposite seasons. «Away from the equator summer days are long and winter days are short», so when it is summer in the UK, it is winter in Australia.
fact: The equator is an imaginary line, so you cannot see it on the ground.
fact: The equator is the line of latitude at 0 degrees.
fact: The equator divides the Earth into the Northern Hemisphere and the Southern Hemisphere.
fact: Near the equator it is hot all year, with no real winter, and days and nights are about the same length.
fact: Kilimanjaro is close to the equator, yet it has snow on top, because the air gets colder the higher you climb.
exercise: Where is the equator? | *An imaginary line halfway between the North Pole and the South Pole | The North Pole | The edge of a map | A road that goes around the world
exercise: The equator splits the Earth into two halves. Which two? | The Hot Half and the Cold Half | The Eastern and Western Hemispheres | The Land and the Sea | *The Northern Hemisphere and the Southern Hemisphere
exercise: Find and copy the number that shows the latitude of the equator. | *0 | 90 | 180 | 45
test: When it is summer in the UK, what season is it in Australia? | Spring | *Winter | Autumn | Summer
test: Why are places near the equator hot all year? | They are near the North Pole | *The Sun is always high in the sky there | The equator is covered in ice | Their days are always short
exam: Which of these is a true fact about the equator? | The equator is a real road you can drive on | *Days and nights are about the same length near it | The equator is the coldest place on Earth | The equator is at 90 degrees latitude
